1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
LASER VAULT HEIST   |   Topic 12   |   OpenGL 3.3 Core

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
An original Blender vault: wood, stone, brass and a cold night window.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
WASD + mouse. Approach the desk lamp and press E.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Interaction 1 / 3: the local lamp changes both its light and visible glow.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Hold CTRL to crouch. The eye height, collision body and rig change together.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Live CCTV: a second camera renders the animated thief into a framebuffer.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Interaction 2 / 3: E switches between two live security views.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Two rotating guard spotlights share their direction with the visible mounts.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:15,000
A deliberate mistake: touching a thin moving laser triggers the alarm.

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:24,000
All illumination turns red. R starts a real reset of the whole attempt.

11
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Actual source + runtime diagnostics. VAO / VBO / EBO and custom GLSL.

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Continuous final attempt: wait for clearance, then cross while crouched.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Laser collision transforms sampled body points into the beam's local box.

14
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:34,000
A rotating beam uses a left-wall pivot. Geometry and collision share its matrix.

15
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:51,000
The controller advances at 240 Hz, including during slow render frames.

16
00:02:51,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Read the next gap. The CCTV keeps rendering while every laser continues moving.

17
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
The last beam requires a crouch. This passage is continuous, without a cut.

18
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Interaction 3 / 3: turn the wheel, retract the bolts, swing the hinged door.

19
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:30,000
VAULT OPENED | Quiet steps. Clean execution.
